    "durationMs": 248407,
    "finalText": "The URL shortener is complete and fully verified. Implementation details:\n\n- **Stack**: axum 0.8.4 + sqlx (PostgreSQL, rustls runtime) + tokio, with `DATABASE_URL` read from the environment.\n- **Schema**: `links` table (`seq BIGSERIAL PK` for creation order, `code TEXT UNIQUE`, `url`, `clicks BIGINT`), applied via an embedded `sqlx::migrate!()` that runs pending migrations at startup before serving — so `sh start.sh` (which execs the prebuilt release binary in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`) applies migrations then serves.\n- **Endpoints**: `POST /links` (201 with `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}`, URL stored unchanged; 409 on duplicate custom code; 422 for malformed JSON/missing url/invalid url/invalid code), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (302 + Location via atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING url`, exactly one click increment; 404 unknown), `GET /links` (`{\"items\",\"total\"}` in ascending creation order). Generated codes are 8 chars from `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` with collision retry; custom codes validated as 4–20 ASCII letters/digits/hyphens/underscores.\n\nAll behaviors were exercised with curl against the live PostgreSQL, including duplicate codes, every 422 path, click-count accuracy, and a full server restart confirming data, click counts, list order, and idempotent migrations all persist. The test server has been stopped and the port is free; the README documents startup with `sh start.sh`."
  }
